{{also|érudition}}
==English==

===Etymology===
{{etydate|15th Century}} From {{der|en|frm|érudition}}, from {{der|en|la|eruditio||an instructing, learning, erudition}}<!--Or "erudition"?-->, from {{m|la|erudire||to instruct, educate, cultivate|lit=free from rudeness}}, from {{m|la|e||out}} + {{m|la|rudis||rude}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌɛɹʊˈdɪʃən/}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-erudition.ogg|Audio (Mid-Atlantic)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# [[profound|Profound]] [[knowledge]] acquired from [[learning]] and [[scholarship]].
# The refinement, polish and knowledge that education confers.

